[{:db/id 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72fa77bc-6d37-516a-bc08-8cef3db1618e" "question-2ce6b951-f687-5e96-9bbc-0957d6d3d0b4" "question-1b086cc6-e229-5377-bb89-5a8ff879bb27" "question-bb9f71b9-54fb-5914-9956-fcba4d5311e6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151870 :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $\\mathcal{P}({B}),$ where $B=\\{1,2,3,4\\}.$\n\n$$\nX \\,R\\, Y \\qquad\\Leftrightarrow\\qquad X \\subseteq Y\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n\n- $R$ is symmetric\n\n- $R$ is transitive\n\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x \\in A,$ $x \\, R\\, x .$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y \\in A,$ if $x \\,R\\, y,$ then $y \\,R\\, x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z \\in A,$ if $x \\,R\\, y$ and $y \\,R\\, z,$ then $x \\,R\\, z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $X \\in \\mathcal{P}({B}),$ $X \\, \\subseteq \\, X .$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $\\{1\\} \\subseteq \\{1,2\\}$ but $\\{1,2\\}  \\not \\subseteq \\{1\\}.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z \\in \\mathcal{P}({B}),$ if $X \\subseteq Y$ and $Y \\subseteq Z,$ then $X \\subseteq Z.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6ee391cd-217d-5ff1-a899-24ea6980b5eb" "question-73719e8c-e17e-53b6-804a-0ade3bbbaa7f" "question-ae54ed26-0094-5420-99d1-1b8455c5d0e3" "question-72d1402f-e4b5-5dff-b1dc-9142e68fa197"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151845 :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A=\\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR=\\big\\{(\\alpha, \\alpha), (\\beta,\\beta), (\\gamma,\\gamma), (\\beta,\\gamma), (\\gamma,\\beta)\\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n\n- $R$ is symmetric\n\n- $R$ is transitive\n\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x \\in A,$ $x \\, R\\, x .$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y \\in A,$ if $x \\,R\\, y,$ then $y \\,R\\, x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z \\in A,$ if $x \\,R\\, y$ and $y \\,R\\, z,$ then $x \\,R\\, z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(\\alpha, \\alpha), (\\beta,\\beta), (\\gamma,\\gamma) \\in R.$$\\:\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x) \\in R$ whenever $(x,y) \\in R.$ $\\:\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in \\{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\},$ if  $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$  then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $({\\color{blue}\\beta},{\\color{red}\\gamma}) \\in R$ and $({\\color{red}\\gamma},{\\color{blue}\\beta})  \\in R,$ and also $({\\color{blue}\\beta},{\\color{blue}\\beta}) \\in R$ $\\:\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- $({\\color{blue}\\gamma},{\\color{red}\\beta}) \\in R$ and $({\\color{red}\\beta},{\\color{blue}\\gamma})  \\in R,$ and also $({\\color{blue}\\gamma},{\\color{blue}\\gamma}) \\in R$ $\\:\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- Since $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, it is an equivalence relation.$\\:\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a3f6ced1-e3e7-51b2-bdb3-c0561413aee0" "question-5c8d639d-4ba9-5766-b837-cc9cfbce29a2" "question-1a65003f-5b78-57dd-8ad6-282231fb787b" "question-0c07a7ee-9fb6-5236-b864-38ec61e9b0cc" "question-78aa39d2-6d95-5a7b-bd86-1b4658d3d903"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151844 :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $\\mathbb{Z}?$\n\n- $a \\not \\mid b$\n\n- $a \\,R\\, b$ if $a - b$ is a multiple of $7$\n\n- $a\\, R \\,b$ if $a \\equiv (b - 1) \\; (\\textrm{mod}\\:5)$" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x \\in A,$ $x \\, R\\, x .$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y \\in A,$ if $x \\,R\\, y,$ then $y \\,R\\, x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z \\in A,$ if $x \\,R\\, y$ and $y \\,R\\, z,$ then $x \\,R\\, z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $1 \\mid 1.$\n\n- Relation II is an equivalence relation. \n\n- It is reflexive because for all $a \\in \\mathbb{Z},$ we have that $a - a=0$ is a multiple of $7.$\n\n- It is symmetric because for all $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z},$ if $a - b$ is a multiple of $7,$ then $b - a=-(a-b)$ is also a multiple of $7.$\n\n- It is transitive because for all $a, b, c \\in \\mathbb{Z},$ if $a - b=7n$ and $b - c=7m,$ where $n, m$ are arbitrary integers, then\n\n$$\na - c = (a - b) + (b - c)=7n+7m=7(n+m)\n$$\n\nThis means that if $a - b$ is a multiple of $7$ and $b - c$ is a multiple of $7$ then $a-c$ is also a multiple of $7.$\n\n- Relation III is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $1 \\not\\equiv (1 - 1) \\; (\\textrm{mod}\\:5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-72fa77bc-6d37-516a-bc08-8cef3db1618e" :question/id #uuid "72fa77bc-6d37-516a-bc08-8cef3db1618e" :question/math-academy-id "q-214252" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $N.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,y∤x\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is not reflexive. For example, $3∣3.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $9∤3$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not transitive. For example, $3∤2$ and $2∤9,$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2eb12818-1e53-50fb-9686-e8410139c5cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2eb12818-1e53-50fb-9686-e8410139c5cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb12818-1e53-50fb-9686-e8410139c5cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-52627dc2-eb63-52a8-8d5f-f961978b8947" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3a23ef4-cc98-56f0-ac39-ae3829545ef5" "answer-7560d387-5026-5568-9eb3-53e8af6d9cef" "answer-0b40b244-4bab-58ee-bc64-fa1d33519579" "answer-5c380eff-8271-5e3c-a697-38aee4ec4cfe" "answer-52627dc2-eb63-52a8-8d5f-f961978b8947"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3a23ef4-cc98-56f0-ac39-ae3829545ef5" :answer/id #uuid "e3a23ef4-cc98-56f0-ac39-ae3829545ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7560d387-5026-5568-9eb3-53e8af6d9cef" :answer/id #uuid "7560d387-5026-5568-9eb3-53e8af6d9cef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b40b244-4bab-58ee-bc64-fa1d33519579" :answer/id #uuid "0b40b244-4bab-58ee-bc64-fa1d33519579" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c380eff-8271-5e3c-a697-38aee4ec4cfe" :answer/id #uuid "5c380eff-8271-5e3c-a697-38aee4ec4cfe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52627dc2-eb63-52a8-8d5f-f961978b8947" :answer/id #uuid "52627dc2-eb63-52a8-8d5f-f961978b8947" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152500 :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A$ containing all possible triangles in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≅y\n$$\n\nRecall that $x≅y$ means that $x$ and $y$ are congruent.\n\nWhich of the following are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $x\\in A,$ we have $x≅x.$ Every triangle is congruent with itself.\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x≅y,$ then $y≅x.$ To see why, note that if we can find a sequence of rigid motions in the plane that maps $x$ to $y$ (implying $x≅y),$ then we can always find a sequence of rigid motions that maps $y$ to $x.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x≅y,$ and $y≅z,$ then $x≅z.$ To see why, note that if we can find a sequence of rigid motions in the plane that maps $x$ to $y$ (implying $x≅y)$ and another sequence that maps $y$ to $z,$ then we can always find a sequence that maps $x$ to $z.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149556 :answer-field/correct 17592186149559 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ce6b951-f687-5e96-9bbc-0957d6d3d0b4" :question/id #uuid "2ce6b951-f687-5e96-9bbc-0957d6d3d0b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-214250" :question/problem "Consider the relation $y∣x$ defined on the set $Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n| The relation is reflexive | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| The relation is symmetric | {{field-2}} |\n| The relation is transitive | {{field-3}} |\n| The relation is an equivalence relation | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is reflexive. For all $x\\in Z,$ $x∣x.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that the relation is symmetric. For example, $1∣2$ but $2∤1.$\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is transitive. For all $x,y,z\\in Z,$ if $y∣x$ and $z∣y,$ then $z∣x.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that this is an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d01c36ca-21c0-59a4-b5b4-403ce3adfc4e" "answer-field-a15825e7-fb6f-53d4-8633-b3346886729b" "answer-field-99b2d851-fde5-5dcf-9ccf-b3176701b14b" "answer-field-ba60e583-f0bb-5d89-9542-b0ca43b9fa37"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d01c36ca-21c0-59a4-b5b4-403ce3adfc4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "d01c36ca-21c0-59a4-b5b4-403ce3adfc4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-5357d66d-1feb-5125-b851-a1faf4d4e579" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36eba4b6-28b6-571d-8217-a141e1dbf8be" "answer-5357d66d-1feb-5125-b851-a1faf4d4e579"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36eba4b6-28b6-571d-8217-a141e1dbf8be" :answer/id #uuid "36eba4b6-28b6-571d-8217-a141e1dbf8be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5357d66d-1feb-5125-b851-a1faf4d4e579" :answer/id #uuid "5357d66d-1feb-5125-b851-a1faf4d4e579" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a15825e7-fb6f-53d4-8633-b3346886729b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a15825e7-fb6f-53d4-8633-b3346886729b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dc2c5cb7-d753-558a-afb1-296e3416064b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc2c5cb7-d753-558a-afb1-296e3416064b" "answer-4831cbaa-092f-5874-8d05-f8dd7f5fc544"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc2c5cb7-d753-558a-afb1-296e3416064b" :answer/id #uuid "dc2c5cb7-d753-558a-afb1-296e3416064b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4831cbaa-092f-5874-8d05-f8dd7f5fc544" :answer/id #uuid "4831cbaa-092f