$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(A),$ $|X|\\,=\\,|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $X,Y\\in P(A),$ if $|X|\\,=\\,|Y|,$ then $|Y|=|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(A),$ if $|X|=|Y|$ and $|Y|=|Z|,$ then $|X|=|Z|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-52a03d34-71d7-5d2a-9d61-7aebbc62d675"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52a03d34-71d7-5d2a-9d61-7aebbc62d675" :answer-field/id #uuid "52a03d34-71d7-5d2a-9d61-7aebbc62d675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3fa9caf0-df86-5322-b028-e17f40231f57" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f67c691-2dcd-52d8-87bc-d5e99dedc4c7" "answer-39fee494-92f8-5270-a473-d2107e7e8874" "answer-3fa9caf0-df86-5322-b028-e17f40231f57" "answer-a05287c6-dfca-5030-894f-a2656886976e" "answer-bffd83c6-f97d-535a-871d-3201a645b707"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f67c691-2dcd-52d8-87bc-d5e99dedc4c7" :answer/id #uuid "6f67c691-2dcd-52d8-87bc-d5e99dedc4c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39fee494-92f8-5270-a473-d2107e7e8874" :answer/id #uuid "39fee494-92f8-5270-a473-d2107e7e8874" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fa9caf0-df86-5322-b028-e17f40231f57" :answer/id #uuid "3fa9caf0-df86-5322-b028-e17f40231f57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a05287c6-dfca-5030-894f-a2656886976e" :answer/id #uuid "a05287c6-dfca-5030-894f-a2656886976e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bffd83c6-f97d-535a-871d-3201a645b707" :answer/id #uuid "bffd83c6-f97d-535a-871d-3201a645b707" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb9f71b9-54fb-5914-9956-fcba4d5311e6" :question/id #uuid "bb9f71b9-54fb-5914-9956-fcba4d5311e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-214254" :question/problem "Consider the relation $X⊆Y$ defined on the set $P(Q).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n| The relation is reflexive | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| The relation is symmetric | {{field-2}} |\n| The relation  is transitive | {{field-3}} |\n| The relation is an equivalence relation | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(Q),$ $X\\,⊆\\,X.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that the relation is symmetric. For example, $N⊆Z$ but $Z⊈N.$\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(Q),$ if $X⊆Y$ and $Y⊆Z,$ then $X⊆Z.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that this is an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-228f10c0-5a8b-5fba-8458-2bce2af4a6eb" "answer-field-8ee9e05d-a1ec-5917-8ee3-429077480b99" "answer-field-c2367340-22dc-5a13-9be5-b192f0b188dc" "answer-field-95f9516a-04fa-5063-891b-2622ee6802d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-228f10c0-5a8b-5fba-8458-2bce2af4a6eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "228f10c0-5a8b-5fba-8458-2bce2af4a6eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4f1f7ce2-0886-55f8-8379-31f971e676b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bbdf36e-3db7-54e8-862b-eb55ec298601" "answer-4f1f7ce2-0886-55f8-8379-31f971e676b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bbdf36e-3db7-54e8-862b-eb55ec298601" :answer/id #uuid "6bbdf36e-3db7-54e8-862b-eb55ec298601" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f1f7ce2-0886-55f8-8379-31f971e676b5" :answer/id #uuid "4f1f7ce2-0886-55f8-8379-31f971e676b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ee9e05d-a1ec-5917-8ee3-429077480b99" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ee9e05d-a1ec-5917-8ee3-429077480b99" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-5e50dec7-66a1-5309-b4d1-3ca325976f1e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e50dec7-66a1-5309-b4d1-3ca325976f1e" "answer-dc973c25-992c-5955-9151-75893641787b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e50dec7-66a1-5309-b4d1-3ca325976f1e" :answer/id #uuid "5e50dec7-66a1-5309-b4d1-3ca325976f1e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc973c25-992c-5955-9151-75893641787b" :answer/id #uuid "dc973c25-992c-5955-9151-75893641787b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2367340-22dc-5a13-9be5-b192f0b188dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2367340-22dc-5a13-9be5-b192f0b188dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8956f580-15e2-5ec6-b015-fe8e0db5e2ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c728c867-0a42-5f45-871c-e98f82f70f08" "answer-8956f580-15e2-5ec6-b015-fe8e0db5e2ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c728c867-0a42-5f45-871c-e98f82f70f08" :answer/id #uuid "c728c867-0a42-5f45-871c-e98f82f70f08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8956f580-15e2-5ec6-b015-fe8e0db5e2ac" :answer/id #uuid "8956f580-15e2-5ec6-b015-fe8e0db5e2ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95f9516a-04fa-5063-891b-2622ee6802d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "95f9516a-04fa-5063-891b-2622ee6802d7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-08f09ac8-e439-549e-86d5-86b2f7775049" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08f09ac8-e439-549e-86d5-86b2f7775049" "answer-57a76793-8553-5922-b416-bfc67112d95c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08f09ac8-e439-549e-86d5-86b2f7775049" :answer/id #uuid "08f09ac8-e439-549e-86d5-86b2f7775049" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57a76793-8553-5922-b416-bfc67112d95c" :answer/id #uuid "57a76793-8553-5922-b416-bfc67112d95c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152502 :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={0,1,2}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(1,1),(0,2),(2,0)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* reflexive because  $(0,0)\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* transitive because $(0,2)\\in R$ and $(2,0)\\in R,$ but $(0,0)\\notin R$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149568 :answer-field/correct 17592186149569 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6ee391cd-217d-5ff1-a899-24ea6980b5eb" :question/id #uuid "6ee391cd-217d-5ff1-a899-24ea6980b5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-214279" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={∗,⋆,∘,⋄}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄),(∗,⋆),(⋆,∗)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in {∗,⋆,∘,⋄},$ if  $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$  then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $(∗,⋆)\\in R$ and $(⋆,∗)\\in R,$ and also $(∗,∗)\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $(⋆,∗)\\in R$ and $(∗,⋆)\\in R,$ and also $(⋆,⋆)\\in R$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Since $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, it is an equivalence relation.$\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aa93e163-1d01-58a1-bdb6-eb95656804a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aa93e163-1d01-58a1-bdb6-eb95656804a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa93e163-1d01-58a1-bdb6-eb95656804a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b40d20c9-3655-52ec-b8aa-91f39c99b226" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce88d57b-0226-5ecc-89db-39d37dd6f50e" "answer-b40d20c9-3655-52ec-b8aa-91f39c99b226" "answer-b81f025c-684f-5d52-9d18-235fa3336997" "answer-c3273c40-cfce-55eb-8615-3692dd6d5895" "answer-6549b369-142b-53da-b553-4facda5dbfe5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce88d57b-0226-5ecc-89db-39d37dd6f50e" :answer/id #uuid "ce88d57b-0226-5ecc-89db-39d37dd6f50e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b40d20c9-3655-52ec-b8aa-91f39c99b226" :answer/id #uuid "b40d20c9-3655-52ec-b8aa-91f39c99b226" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b81f025c-684f-5d52-9d18-235fa3336997" :answer/id #uuid "b81f025c-684f-5d52-9d18-235fa3336997" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3273c40-cfce-55eb-8615-3692dd6d5895" :answer/id #uuid "c3273c40-cfce-55eb-8615-3692dd6d5895" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6549b369-142b-53da-b553-4facda5dbfe5" :answer/id #uuid "6549b369-142b-53da-b553-4facda5dbfe5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-73719e8c-e17e-53b6-804a-0ade3bbbaa7f" :question/id #uuid "73719e8c-e17e-53b6-804a-0ade3bbbaa7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-214273" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={a,b,c}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(a,a),(b,b),(c,c),(a,b),(b,a),(b,c),(c,b)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(a,a),\\,(b,b),\\,(c,c)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* transitive because $(a,b)\\in R$ and $(b,c)\\in R,$ but $(a,c)\\notin R$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e2bbacab-cf91-5eed-be7e-c39a7e7d8711"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2bbacab-cf91-5eed-be7e-c39a7e7d8711" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2bbacab-cf91-5eed-be7e-c39a7e7d8711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9dfb0cac-6b03-5126-9a12-63bea663b5bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9dfb0cac-6b03-5126-9a12-63bea663b5bb" "answer-0327b892-d3d1-5fb3-b2f0-3b4c1f296dde" "answer-3aa8f00c-f005-593e-8e78-a866a0839afc" "answer-9161f808-0aca-580f-99a3-789451a1123e" "answer-6ff811d1-d506-5b23-8e83-bc217090e57c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9dfb0cac-6b03-5126-9a12-63bea663b5bb" :answer/id #uuid "9dfb0cac-6b03-5126-9a12-63bea663b5bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0327b892-d3d1-5fb3-b2f0-3b4c1f296dde" :answer/id #uuid "0327b892-d3d1-5fb3-b2f0-3b4c1f296dde" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3aa8f00c-f005-593e-8e78-a866a0839afc" :answer/id #uuid "3aa8f00c-f005-593e-8e78-a866a0839afc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9161f808-0aca-580f-99a3-789451a1123e" :answer/id #uuid "9161f808-0aca-580f-99a3-789451a1123e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ff811d1-d506-5b23-8e83-bc217090e57c" :answer/id #uuid "6ff811d1-d506-5b23-8e83-bc217090e57c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae54ed26-0094-5420-99d1-1b8455c5d0e3" :question/id #uuid "ae54ed26-0094-5420-99d1-1b8455c5d0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-214280" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta }$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\alpha ,\\beta ),(\\beta ,\\beta )}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* symmetric because $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R$ but $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because it contains no \"linked\" pairs such that $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R.\\,✓$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-175e3445-e959-5d80-ae1e-e6de0e0b369c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-175e3445-e959-5d80-ae1e-e6de0e0b369c" :answer-field/id #uuid "175e3445-e959-5d80-ae1e-e6de0e0b369c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b7315505-3d31-5c27-bce8-fce3301ee94f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b7315505-3d31-5c27-bce8-fce3301ee94f" "answer-1f9f9465-cf5d-580a-9ff3-750b6c28f614" "answer-9a50ef14-e242-54e6-8842-59f1b35210fa" "answer-51f10fd9-b7c9-54fc-a041-a40a299e4aa8" "answer-dc8d78e5-cb92-5ee7-9999-50c90b8b56ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7315505-3d31-5c27-bce8-fce3301ee94f" :answer/id #uuid "b7315505-3d31-5c27-bce8-fce3301ee94f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f9f9465-cf5d-580a-9ff3-750b6c28f614" :answer/id #uuid "1f9f9465-cf5d-580a-9ff3-750b6c28f614" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a50ef14-e242-54e6-8842-59f1b35210fa" :answer/id #uuid "9a50ef14-e242-54e6-8842-59f1b35210